** ======================================================================
** CBM_HIGHDIP_MFVW  X1  v10  = source corrected to 煤炭科学技术 (Coal Sci & Tech)
** Wang Hongli et al. 2021, 'Numerical simulation of CBM leakage in shallow exposed area
** of high-dip coal seams', doi:10.13199/j.cnki.cst.2020-1683. Table2 ORIGINAL (pre-HM) column:
**   thickness 18 m, dip 45, k=7 mD, aniso 5 -> kz=1.4, frac phi=0.75%, matrix phi=15.25%,
**   gas content 8.35 m3/t, grad 0.009, ref 6000 kPa @700m, P-grad 9.42 kPa/m, rockcomp 1.8e-5,
**   Langmuir VL=36.116 m3/t, PL=4.299 MPa(=4299 kPa).
** FULL-SIZE (original) domain 80x100x15m. For BHP extraction: import X1 daily production
**   (X1_production_import.csv) as rate constraint; read back well BHP from .sr3.
** v15: RATE-CONTROLLED on 312m domain (=v14) to EXTRACT flowing BHP.
**   Impose X1 measured water(STW)+gas(STG) as rate ceilings, BHP floor 50 kPa (non-binding).
**   Early: gas supply-limited (undersat, P>1293) -> water ceiling binds; later gas ceiling binds.
**   Read BHP from .sr3 = the flowing pressure consistent with X1 production. Verify ALTER/OPERATE in Builder.
** v14: = v13 physics (CoalSciTech params + ADSTAB undersaturation + Sw=1.0) BUT domain
**   shrunk 1200x1500m -> 315x315m (=312m real X1 spacing), 18m thick, well centered 11,11 K=1:10.
**   Rationale: full domain cannot dewater below crit desorption 1293 kPa -> zero gas (v13).
**   Smaller drainage lets dewatering drop P<1293 in ~2yr -> desorption gas ramp like X1.
** v13: = v12 + initial Sw=1.0 (fully water-saturated cleats, NO initial free gas;
**   gas can only come from matrix desorption below crit desorption 1293 kPa).
** v12: UNDERSATURATION via tabular ADSTAB isotherm. Table plateaus at 8.35 m3/t (=0.35247 gmol/kg)
**   from 6000 down to crit desorption ~1293 kPa, then Langmuir(VL=36.116,PL=4299) below.
**   Equilibrium init @6000 kPa reads 8.35 m3/t off the table (correct undersaturated content);
**   no gas desorbs until dewatering drops P below ~1293 kPa -> reproduces the ~2yr gas delay.
**   ADSTAB format + 2-rock-type (matrix sorbs, fracture inert) per Dorothy's Sihe deck.
** ======================================================================
RESULTS SIMULATOR GEM 201910


TITLE1 'CBM_X1_v15_rateControl_BHPextract'
INUNIT SI
WSRF WELL TIME
WSRF GRID TIME
REWIND 2
WRST 365
OUTSRF GRID ADS 'CH4' ADS 'CO2' POROS PRES SG SW TGIP Y 'CH4' Y 'CO2' ZFACG
OUTSRF RES NONE
WPRN GRID 0
OUTPRN GRID NONE
OUTPRN RES NONE
**  Distance units: m 
RESULTS XOFFSET           0.0000
RESULTS YOFFSET           0.0000
RESULTS ROTATION           0.0000  **  (DEGREES)
RESULTS AXES-DIRECTIONS 1.0 -1.0 1.0
** ***************************************************************************
** Definition of fundamental cartesian grid
** ***************************************************************************
GRID VARI 21 21 10
KDIR DOWN
DI IVAR 
 21*15
DJ JVAR 
 21*15
DK ALL 
 4410*1.800000
DTOP
 21*541.0000 21*556.0000 21*571.0000 21*586.0000 21*601.0000
 21*616.0000 21*631.0000 21*646.0000 21*661.0000 21*676.0000
 21*691.0000 21*706.0000 21*721.0000 21*736.0000 21*751.0000
 21*766.0000 21*781.0000 21*796.0000 21*811.0000 21*826.0000
 21*841.0000
DUALPOR 
SHAPE WR
DIFRAC CON 2.00
DJFRAC CON 2.00
DKFRAC CON 2.00
NULL *FRACTURE CON 1
NULL *MATRIX CON 1
** Total porosity 0.015 split: inherited cleat 0.0005 + matrix 0.0145.
POR *FRACTURE CON 0.00750
POR *MATRIX CON 0.15250
** cleat (fracture-continuum) permeability, mD
PERMI *FRACTURE CON 7.000
PERMJ *FRACTURE CON 7.000
PERMK *FRACTURE CON 1.400
PERMI *MATRIX CON 0.001000
PERMJ *MATRIX CON 0.001000
PERMK *MATRIX CON 0.000100
PINCHOUTARRAY CON 1
PRPOR FRACTURE 6000.0
PRPOR MATRIX 6000.0
CPOR FRACTURE 1.80e-05
CPOR MATRIX 1.80e-05

** ============================== COMPONENTS (PR EOS) ====================
** 2-component CO2+CH4 (template); CO2 inert here -> pure CH4 depletion.
MODEL PR
NC 2 2
COMPNAME 'CO2' 'CH4'
HCFLAG
0 1
TRES 20.07
MW
44.01 16.043
AC
0.225 0.008
PCRIT          ** atm
72.8 45.4
VCRIT
0.094 0.099
TCRIT          ** K
304.2 190.6
PCHOR
78 77
SG
0.818 0.3
TB
-78.45 -161.45
HEATING_VALUES
0 212.758
VISVC
0.094 0.099
BIN
0.103
DENW 960.2   ** gives ~9.42 kPa/m gradient (Table2)
REFPW 101.325
VISW 0.7

